      <div type="clause" n="36.1a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 36.1a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 36.1a" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="566" ed="#liebermann"/>Nemo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="r" target="#Hn_36-1a.lnote.oe.r"/> enim<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Hn_36-1a.lnote.oe.34"/> ouerseunessam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Hn_36-1a.lnote.oe.13"/> sui ipsius habet, set fortasse dominus eius.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 566 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_36-1a.lnote.oe.r" n="r" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">566</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">36, 1<hi rend="italic">a erklärt, wieso Overseunessa häufig von Rechtswegen nicht existirt; ebenso</hi> 24, 1. <hi rend="italic">Zu</hi> Nemo <hi rend="italic">schreibt Corr. an den Rand:</hi> s&lt;sup&gt;u&lt;/sup&gt;. e . C . [<hi rend="italic">d. h.</hi> sumitur e contra?] super barones <hi rend="italic">Sc; genau so roth am Rande Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">36, 1a explains why the overseunessa frequently does not exist by right; similarly 24, 1. Beside Nemo the corrector writes in the margin: s&lt;sup&gt;u&lt;/sup&gt;. e . C . [i.e. sumitur e contra?] super barones Sc; exactly the same in red in the margin Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_36-1a.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">566</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-senn. <hi rend="italic">stets Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-senn. <hi rend="italic">always Co</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_36-1a.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">566</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lond</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
